@page "/about"

<div class="about-page">

    <h1>About LocalExpenser</h1>

    <p>
        LocalExpenser is a personal expense tracking application designed to help
        users manage and organize their daily expenses in a simple and efficient way.
    </p>

    <p>
        The application was built as a learning project to explore modern
        <strong>.NET</strong> development using <strong>Blazor</strong>, while
        implementing real-world features such as authentication, database management,
        and application architecture.
    </p>

    <h2>Features</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Add, edit, and delete expenses</li>
        <li>Search, filter, and sort expenses</li>
        <li>Filter expenses by category and date</li>
        <li>View expense statistics through a dashboard</li>
        <li>User registration and authentication</li>
        <li>Protected pages using authorization</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Technology</h2>

    <p>
        LocalExpenser is built using:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>ASP.NET Core</li>
        <li>Blazor Web App</li>
        <li>C#</li>
        <li>Entity Framework Core</li>
        <li>MySQL</li>
        <li>ASP.NET Core Identity</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Architecture</h2>

    <p>
        The application follows a layered architecture where Blazor components
        handle the user interface, services contain business logic, Entity Framework
        Core manages data access, and MySQL stores application data.
    </p>

    <h2>Purpose</h2>

    <p>
        This project was created to practice building modern web applications with
        .NET and Blazor, including component-based UI development, dependency
        injection, database migrations, authentication, and authorization.
    </p>

    <p>
        Thank you for using LocalExpenser.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <footer class="about-footer">
        <p>
            Version 1.0.0<br />
            Built with ❤️ using .NET and Blazor
        </p>
    </footer>
</div>
